# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, the working-tree form of every file is whatever each
# clone's core.autocrlf happens to be. Git for Windows defaults that to true,
# so a Windows clone of this public repo would rewrite the Windows configs and
# produce phantom diffs. Declaring the intent here makes it deterministic.
#
# Git stores every text file as LF; the working-tree form is decided below.

* text=auto

# Windows-native configs. chezmoi copies these byte-for-byte (none of them are
# templates), and the tools that consume them — komorebi, yasb, whkd, Windows
# Terminal, PowerShell — are CRLF-native.
dot_config/windows/** text eol=crlf

# Encrypted payloads are opaque even though age armor is ASCII: the armor is
# line-oriented and must never be rewritten.
*.age -text
